<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Identity ability over text: the bot's sense of its own name. The body (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) invokes it
  as its child "identity".

    recalling -bot.ability.identity.recalled-> knowing {
      listening -heard text-> recognizing.recognized -> listening
      listening -environment.sound-> recognizing.classifying (speech
        decoding) -> recognized -> listening }
    knowing -bot.ability.identity.adopt-> adopting
      -bot.ability.identity.adopted-> knowing

  A bot is born nameless: nothing in the body supplies a name. name is the
  invoker's <param name="name"> when it passes one (tests do; the body does
  not), else null.

  recalling: with a database (the <param>
  database, the memory database file) it invokes the memory ability
  (abilities/memory/memory.scx) to select the adopted names (query_tags
  self_name, subject_ref self, oldest first, at most 50) and sends
  bot.ability.identity.recalled {name} to #_internal with the last one
  that decodes as a name ({text, kind?}, kind "fact" when absent, no other key, text of 1 to 64
  characters; a damaged row is skipped, so it never costs the bot the name
  adopted before it), else
  with the name the session started with ({text, kind: "fact"}, or null). A memory that does not answer
  yet is a peer still coming up, not an empty one: an attempt that fails (logged as identity.recall.failed,
  "Identity could not recall a name from memory: ...") or does not answer
  within recall_attempt_timeout_ms (1 s) is asked again after
  recall_retry_delay_ms (100 ms). When the bring-up budget
  (bring_up_timeout_ms, the <param>, 30 s by default; the body passes
  half its activation_timeout_ms) runs out first, it
  sends bot.ability.failed {message: "Identity could not recall a name:
  memory did not answer within the bring-up budget."} to the parent and
  recalls the session's name.
  Without a database it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"> and
  recalls the session's name.

  Asking:
  bot.ability.identity.ask {} while knowing is answered with
  bot.ability.identity.named {name} (the name the bot answers to, or null)
  to the parent; the body relays the cognition's ask here and the answer
  back to the cognition. An ask that arrives while recalling or adopting
  is deferred, so it is never answered "none" too early. Every adoption
  also sends named to the parent once the name is taken.

  Recognition: identity is one
  of the body's input abilities, so each environment.sound reaches it;
  with a name to look for, classifying invokes
  abilities/speech_decoding/speech_decoding.scx on the sound and
  <identity:hears_name> looks for the name in the transcript (no transcript
  leaves the ability). A decoding failure answers the body with
  bot.ability.failed {message} and goes back to listening. Text (decision
  D43): the
  body also relays each outside bot.ability.communication.input to this
  ability. <identity:hears_name> decides whether its text (a string content with
  a text/* content_type) names the bot: the name's case-folded
  letter-and-digit tokens appear as a whole run in the text's (so a bot
  named "Al" is not addressed by "always"). Addressed: the body gets
  bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus} whose stimulus is
  bot.ability.identity.addressed {name} from "identity", and grants it a
  turn. Not addressed, or no name yet, produces nothing: a
  nameless bot only hears words. Other communication content is not
  heard.

  Adoption: bot.ability.identity.adopt {name, reason?} is offered (as the
  model-callable act of taking a name) on every entry into knowing,
  through <decision:choice events="bot.ability.identity.adopt"
  effort="adopt_effort"> (its effort, 1 by default, decision D206), made
  model-facing by <processing:model_facing_schema> ($schema, title and
  examples dropped), in
  bot.ability.offers {ability: "identity", choices}, from knowing's
  onentry (<decision:choice> reads knowing's own transitions there,
  before a child is entered); the first offers are the ability's
  readiness. adopting writes the name down before answering to
  it: with a database it inserts the name (scope long_term, kind fact,
  query_tags self_name, subject_ref self, and the recall orders ties in
  created_at by memory_id, so two adoptions in one second keep their
  order) and sends
  bot.ability.identity.adopted {name: {text, kind: "fact"}} to
  #_internal; a write that fails answers the body with bot.ability.failed
  {message: "Identity could not remember the name it took: ..."} (taken
  in one transition: a private event sent to #_internal would be judged by the adopt
  transition, whose descriptor matches it) and the bot keeps its old name
  (fail-closed).
  Without a database it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"> and
  sends adopted.

  Deferral: communication input, sounds, adopt and
  ask events that arrive while recalling or adopting, and input and sounds that
  arrive while recognizing, are held by <event:defer/> (scxml.rs
  namespaces/event) and come back, in order, once the configuration
  changes, so knowing (or listening, after recognizing) takes each by the
  same transitions as on arrival.

  Logs: identity.name (each name taken, recalled or adopted),
  identity.recall.failed (each recall attempt that failed),
  identity.heard (whether a relayed text addressed the bot), and
  identity.offers.

  Contracts: every event it takes names its abilities/schemas/ file by
  event:schema. A send or raise whose data does not satisfy it is
  error.execution in its sender, and input from outside the session that
  does not is refused, so no cond rechecks a payload.

  Bindings: the bot, decision, identity and processing namespace packages and the memory ability's
  sql service package (a run grants it its directory: scx run's dir option).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:identity="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/identity"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="identity" initial="recalling">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- How heavy an action bot.ability.identity.adopt is (decision D206),
         which the cognition holds against each tier's effort ceiling.
         Taking a name is never a reflex: the decision layer (ceiling 0)
         holds it, and intuition (ceiling 1) and reasoning may take it. An
         invoker's <param> sets it. -->
    <data id="adopt_effort" expr="1"/>
    <data id="name" expr="null"/>
    <data id="addressed" expr="false"/>
    <!-- The sound in hand while classifying. -->
    <data id="heard" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The addressed stimulus envelope, for the handoff. -->
    <data id="handoff" expr="null"/>
    <data id="adopting_name" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The offers. -->
    <data id="offered" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="offers_over" expr="false"/>
    <!-- Memory: the database file (null: no memory) and its statements.
         The SQL runs on both
         engines (SQLite and Postgres). A memory id is the next row count
         as 32 zero-padded digits (neither engine's randomness is unique
         across invocations in Wasm); JSON rows are told by their
         content_format, the 50 most recent by created_at,
         then memory_id (the insertion order), read oldest first. -->
    <data id="database" expr="null"/>
    <data id="name_select" expr="'SELECT content FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id FROM bot_memory WHERE query_tags = ?1 AND subject_ref = ?2 AND content_format = \'application/json\' ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC LIMIT 50) AS recent ORDER BY created_at, memory_id'"/>
    <data id="name_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_memory (memory_id, scope, context_ref, subject_ref, kind, sensitivity, retention, content, content_format, query_tags) VALUES ((SELECT substr(\'00000000000000000000000000000000\', 1, 32 - length(n)) || n FROM (SELECT CAST(COUNT(*) + 1 AS TEXT) AS n FROM bot_memory) AS c), ?1, NULL, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7, ?8)'"/>
    <data id="recalled_name" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Recall's time bounds: one attempt, the pause before the next, and
         the bring-up budget (30 s; the body passes half its
         activation_timeout_ms, so the budget runs out first),
         which an invoker may set as a <param>. -->
    <data id="recall_attempt_timeout_ms" expr="1000"/>
    <data id="recall_retry_delay_ms" expr="100"/>
    <data id="bring_up_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="name_parameters" expr="[]"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="identity.js"/>

  <!-- Wake up remembering the name, when there is a memory to have
       remembered it in; else the name the session started with. -->
  <state id="recalling" initial="recalling_from">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="recalled_name" expr="recalledName()"/>
    </onentry>
    <state id="recalling_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoDatabase()" target="recalling_nothing"/>
      <transition target="recalling_memory"/>
    </state>
    <state id="recalling_nothing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.identity.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="name" expr="recalled_name"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
    </state>
    <!-- A memory that does not answer yet is not an empty one: an attempt that fails or takes
         longer than recall_attempt_timeout_ms is asked again after
         recall_retry_delay_ms, until the bring-up budget runs out. -->
    <state id="recalling_memory" initial="asking">
      <onentry>
        <send id="recalling-memory-after" event="recalling_memory.after" delayexpr="delay(bring_up_timeout_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="recalling-memory-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <state id="asking">
        <onentry>
          <send id="asking-after" event="asking.after" delayexpr="delay(recall_attempt_timeout_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="asking-after"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="recall" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
          <param name="database" expr="database"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="nameSelectStatements()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
          <assign location="recalled_name" expr="recalledNameFromMemory(_event)"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.identity.recalled" target="#_internal">
            <param name="name" expr="recalled_name"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="waiting">
          <log label="identity.recall.failed" expr="recallFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="asking.after" target="waiting">
          <log label="identity.recall.failed" expr="'Identity could not recall a name from memory: memory did not answer in time.'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <state id="waiting">
        <onentry>
          <send id="waiting-after" event="waiting.after" delayexpr="delay(recall_retry_delay_ms)"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="waiting-after"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="waiting.after" target="asking"/>
      </state>
      <!-- The bring-up budget ran out with memory still not answering:
           wake with the session's name, and say so. -->
      <transition event="recalling_memory.after">
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="'Identity could not recall a name: memory did not answer within the bring-up budget.'"/>
        </send>
        <send event="bot.ability.identity.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="name" expr="recalled_name"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../schemas/environment.sound.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.adopt" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.adopt.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <!-- An ask waits for the name the bot woke up with, so it is never
         answered "none" too early. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.ask" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.ask.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.recalled" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.recalled.json" target="knowing">
      <assign location="name" expr="recalledNameText(_event)"/>
      <log label="identity.name" expr="recalledNameLog()"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <state id="knowing" initial="listening">
    <!-- The offers, read on entry: the choices are knowing's own
         transitions, since no child is entered yet. -->
    <onentry>
      <decision:choice location="offered" events="bot.ability.identity.adopt" effort="adopt_effort"/>
      <processing:model_facing_schema location="offered" bound="32768" overlocation="offers_over"/>
      <if cond="offers_over">
        <log label="identity.offers.dropped" expr="'the offers are over 32768 bytes'"/>
      </if>
      <log label="identity.offers" expr="offered"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.offers" target="#_parent">
        <param name="ability" expr="'identity'"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="offered"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <!-- Offered for the whole time the ability is knowing: a bot can be
         given a name mid-sentence. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.adopt" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.adopt.json" target="adopting">
      <assign location="adopting_name" expr="_event.data.name"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Tell the asker the name the bot answers to, or that it has none
         yet: a reply to the parent, never a broadcast. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.ask" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.ask.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.identity.named" target="#_parent">
        <param name="name" expr="name"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <state id="listening">
      <!-- A nameless bot hears words and nothing follows from them. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json"
                  cond="canRecognize()" target="recognized">
        <identity:hears_name location="addressed" name="name" text="heardText(_event.data)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../schemas/environment.sound.json"
                  cond="canRecognize()" target="classifying">
        <assign location="heard" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- One recognition decision about one heard text or sound. -->
    <state id="recognizing" initial="recognized">
      <!-- Input that arrives meanwhile waits. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../schemas/environment.sound.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>

      <!-- Recognition: decode the sound, then look for
           the name in the transcript; no transcript leaves this state. -->
      <state id="classifying">
        <invoke id="speech_decoding" type="scxml" src="../speech_decoding/speech_decoding.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="heard.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="heard.media_type"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_decoding" cond="hasTranscript(_event)" target="recognized">
          <identity:hears_name location="addressed" name="name" text="_event.data.text"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_decoding" target="listening">
          <log label="identity.recognition.failed" expr="recognitionFailedMessage(_event)"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="recognitionFailedMessage(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="listening">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="recognitionErrorMessage(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <state id="recognized">
        <transition cond="addressed" target="listening">
          <log label="identity.heard" expr="addressedLog()"/>
          <assign location="handoff" expr="({})"/>
          <assign location="handoff.event" expr="'bot.ability.identity.addressed'"/>
          <assign location="handoff.data" expr="({})"/>
          <assign location="handoff.data.name" expr="name"/>
          <assign location="handoff.source" expr="'identity'"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
            <param name="stimulus" expr="handoff"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition target="listening">
          <log label="identity.heard" expr="'not addressed'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- Take the selected name and write it down before answering to it
       (fail-closed: a name that could not be written down is not taken). -->
  <state id="adopting" initial="adopting_from">
    <state id="adopting_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoDatabase()" target="adopting_nothing"/>
      <transition target="adopting_memory"/>
    </state>
    <state id="adopting_nothing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.identity.adopted" target="#_internal">
          <param name="name" expr="adoptedName()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
    </state>
    <state id="adopting_memory">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="name_parameters" expr="nameInsertParameters()"/>
        <assign location="name_parameters" expr="nameInsertParametersCompleted()"/>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="remember" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="statements" expr="nameInsertStatements()"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.identity.adopted" target="#_internal">
          <param name="name" expr="adoptedName()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- The write failed (taken here: a failure sent to #_internal would
           be judged by the adopt descriptor,
           which matches it, and refused). -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="knowing">
        <log label="identity.adopt.failed" expr="adoptFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="adoptFailedMessage(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.adopted" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.adopted.json" target="knowing">
      <assign location="name" expr="_event.data.name.text"/>
      <log label="identity.name" expr="adoptedNameLog()"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.identity.named" target="#_parent">
        <param name="name" expr="name"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../schemas/environment.sound.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.adopt" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.adopt.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.ask" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.ask.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
